OpenCMR2 for AmigaOS 3.2 / PiStorm
==================================

A native AmigaOS port of OpenCMR2, a reimplementation of the engine of
Colin McRae Rally 2.0. It needs the original PC game data; none is included.

Contents
--------

  opencmr2                    the game
  opencmr2.info               its Workbench icon
  Libs/minigl.library         MiniGL 29.1, the version the game is built for
  shaders/                    compiled shaders for the GLES2 renderer
  LICENSE                     OpenCMR2 licence (GNU GPL version 3)
  License_MiniGL_Library.txt  MiniGL licence

Requirements
------------

  - AmigaOS 3.2
  - PiStorm on a Raspberry Pi 4 / CM4 (68040 + FPU build; tested on the
    68060 PAL setup)
  - RTG with a 32-bit screen mode, 640x480 or larger
  - AHI (no AHI means no sound)
  - optional, for the GLES2 renderer: ogles2.library 1.3.3 or newer
  - the original PC installation of Colin McRae Rally 2.0

Installing
----------

1. Copy Libs/minigl.library to LIBS:.
2. Make a COPY of the PC installation on an Amiga drive. Do not use your
   only copy: the Amiga version writes its settings and driver profiles in
   its own format, which the PC version cannot read (and the other way
   round). Saved games are kept apart from PC saves.
3. Copy opencmr2, opencmr2.info and the shaders drawer into that copy,
   next to the game data.
4. Start the game from its icon, or from a Shell in that drawer:

     opencmr2

   The first start resets the game's configuration once. This is expected.

Settings
--------

PROGDIR:opencmr2.ini holds the port's settings; the game's own options are
set in its menus.

  [video]
  fullscreen = 1
  renderer = minigl
  cube_faces_per_frame = 1

  fullscreen            1 opens a screen, 0 a window on Workbench.
  renderer              minigl or gles2. gles2 needs ogles2.library; the
                        game falls back to minigl when GLES2 cannot start.
  cube_faces_per_frame  gles2 only: how many faces (1-6) of the car's
                        reflection map are redrawn each frame. 6 is the
                        original behaviour and is slow.

The game is played with the keyboard; the mouse is not used. Ctrl-C in the
Shell, or the window's close gadget, quits like the menu's Quit.

Problems
--------

The game writes PROGDIR:opencmr2.log. Please include it with any report.

